  "title": "Wrap up my PGC Nordics 2026",
  "date": "2026-10-21T21:00:00.000Z",
  "content": "Wrap up my PGC Nordics 2026\n\nGrandpa's bee haven on PGC\n\nCome and play Grandpa's Bee Haven, only 6.99 EUR.\n\nLast two days, I was in Helsinki attending Pocket Gamers Connect. As Grandpa's Bee Haven is selected in The Big Indie Pitch.\n\nPGC Nordics\n\nNew trends\n\n\n\nThe first day of the event is about marketing. How to make UA(User Aquisition) and D2C(Direct to customers). Some how TV party games is more focused in these talks. It might be the TV games are becoming a trend, or because Netflix is one of the sponsor.\n\nPlay Testing\n\n\n\nIn the indie game show, I played\n\nBook of Infinity: 1001 Nights,\n\nGulltatrophy.\n\nCat Craft,\n\nPurr-suit of Happiness.\n\nRail Jam\n\nTimoS\n\nTrainimals\n\nGame Couch\n\nNothing Normal\n\nFootball Parents\n\nPractical AI\n\nThere are talks about using AI to make games and making assets. Although it is AI week in Helsinki. There is no big companies like Google show up.\n\nQA\n\n\n\nAltTester has a good talk about using it to do integration test\n\nCity walk in Helsinki\n\nI always think that the inflation in Estonia makes everything 1.5 - 2x more expansive. It turns out that it is the same in Helsinki.\n\nDawn in Helsinki shows a strong loneliness feeling of scandinavian style. Although Helsinki has more population than Tallinn.\n\n| | | | |\n|-|-|-|-|\n| ||||",
